<title>MONACO: SQUASH-FITZ-GERALD ENDS JACKMAN RUN TO WIN MONTE CARLO TITLE.</title>
<headline>SQUASH-FITZ-GERALD ENDS JACKMAN RUN TO WIN MONTE CARLO TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Sarah Fitz-Gerald ended the giant-killing run of Cassie Jackman when she beat the English player 9-4 9-2 4-9 9-6 in the final of the Monte Carlo women's squash classic on Saturday.</p>
<p>After upsetting former world number one Michelle Martin of Australia on Friday, Jackman could manage only one game from Fitz-Gerald.</p>
<p>The Australian world champion overcame a stuttering third game to clinch the match in 53 minutes.</p>
</text>
